/-!
# Consequences of the shadow law: the primitive defect and the compression ledger

The differential rank of an entire function is the transcendence degree over `ℂ` of the field
generated by the coordinate and all its jets; its shadow rank is the same for the derivatives of
positive order only.  The difference is the *primitive defect*, and it is zero or one, because the
full jet family is the shadow family together with the single further element `u`.

The shadow law then says that composing with an autonomous first-order cap makes the new rank the
old shadow rank plus one.  Iterating along a chain of caps gives the compression ledger: the rank
after `N` caps is the initial rank plus `N` minus the defects met along the way.
-/

